course: dictionary
lesson: 6177
title: A monster in a maze
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A name like Minotaur is the name of one special character, and it starts with a capital letter. You can often work out who it is from the words around it. «Theseus and the Minotaur» tells you the Minotaur is a character who meets a hero in a story.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The Minotaur is a myth, but bull-leaping was a real sport or ritual of the Minoans.» The word myth is a clue. A myth is an old story that is not true. The word but shows a contrast: the Minotaur is not real, unlike the bull-leaping, which was real.
explain: The other clues describe it: a monster with a man's body and a bull's head, living in a maze called the Labyrinth. Monster and maze both hint at danger. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: The Minotaur is a monster in Greek myths.
fact: It has the body of a man and the head of a bull.
fact: It lived in the Labyrinth, a maze on the island of Crete.
fact: The hero Theseus killed the Minotaur with help from Ariadne's thread.
fact: A myth is an old story that is not literally true, though it may have heroes, gods or monsters in it.
exercise: «The Minotaur lived in a maze called the Labyrinth.» What is the Minotaur? | A king of Crete who loved mazes | A sport where people jumped over bulls | A hero who sailed across the sea | *A monster in a Greek myth, with a man's body and a bull's head
exercise: Pupil says the Minotaur is a real animal kept in a zoo. What do the words «Greek myths» suggest? | It is a sport played in Greece today | It is a new film about a zoo | It is a real bull kept in a zoo | *It is a made-up creature from an old story
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means an old story that is not true: «The Minotaur is a myth, but bull-leaping was a real sport or ritual of the Minoans.» | ritual | Minoans | *myth | sport
test: «The Minotaur lived in a maze called the Labyrinth.» Where did the Minotaur live? | In a river | In a palace garden | On a ship | *In a maze called the Labyrinth
test: «Modern films and books change these old myths a lot to make new stories.» What is a myth? | *An old story, not literally true | A true story from last year | A kind of maze | A type of film
exam: In the sentence «The Minotaur is a myth, but bull-leaping was a real sport», what does the word but show? | It is a question about the Minoans | *A contrast: the Minotaur is not real, but the sport was | It means the sport is not real | It adds more information about the Minotaur
